---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const blogHref = `${base}/blog`.replace('//', '/');
---
<BaseLayout title="Connor Atkins">
  <h1>Connor Atkins</h1>
  <p class="tagline">Token engineering. Time to build.</p>

  <p>
    I'm a PhD researcher working on uncertainty-guided multi-resolution
    classification of whole slide images — teaching neural networks to grade
    colorectal cancer the way a pathologist actually does, zooming in only
    when the tissue is ambiguous. My thesis combines multiple-instance
    learning, foundation-model features, and knowledge distillation across
    magnifications.
  </p>

  <p>
    Outside the lab I build agents. I'm interested in what happens when you
    treat tokens as the unit of economic output — the shape of the tools,
    harnesses, and interfaces that let small teams ship disproportionately.
    Most of that work is public on GitHub; the rest will end up on this blog.
  </p>

  <p>
    Currently based in the UK. Always happy to talk about computational
    pathology, agent engineering, or poker.
  </p>

  <nav class="nav">
    <a href={blogHref}>Blog</a>
    <a href="#" aria-disabled="true" title="Coming soon">About</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/connor113" rel="me noopener">GitHub</a>
    <a href="https://twitter.com/ConnorAtkins11" rel="me noopener">Twitter</a>
  </nav>
</BaseLayout>
